From: okhsunrog <me@okhsunrog.ru>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/ttm: add missing ttm_resource_del_bulk_move_unevictable() definition

CachyOS 7.0.10-1 cherry-picked commit 1d59f36e95f7 ("drm/ttm: Fix
ttm_bo_shrink() infinite LRU walk on backup failure") which calls
ttm_resource_del_bulk_move_unevictable(), but the function definition
was not included. Add it.

Unlike ttm_resource_del_bulk_move() which skips unevictable resources,
this variant unconditionally removes the resource from its bulk_move,
for use after a resource has become unevictable (e.g. after successful
backup/swap).

Signed-off-by: okhsunrog <me@okhsunrog.ru>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/ttm/ttm_resource.c
@@ -293,6 +293,14 @@ void ttm_resource_del_bulk_move(struct t
 		ttm_lru_bulk_move_del(bo->bulk_move, res);
 }

+/* Remove the resource from a bulk move unconditionally (for unevictable resources) */
+void ttm_resource_del_bulk_move_unevictable(struct ttm_resource *res,
+					    struct ttm_buffer_object *bo)
+{
+	if (bo->bulk_move)
+		ttm_lru_bulk_move_del(bo->bulk_move, res);
+}
+
 /* Move a resource to the LRU or bulk tail */
 void ttm_resource_move_to_lru_tail(struct ttm_resource *res)
 {
